WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.694
Welcome to Grade 3 English, Unit
8: Numbers, Shapes, and Measurement.

2
00:00:04.774 --> 00:00:08.983
In this unit you use English to talk about maths in real life.

3
00:00:09.063 --> 00:00:13.273
You count and name big numbers, all the way up to one million.

4
00:00:13.353 --> 00:00:18.185
You learn the words addition,
subtraction, multiplication and division.

5
00:00:18.265 --> 00:00:25.795
You measure the size, height, weight and distance of
things around you, using words like metre and centimetre.

6
00:00:25.875 --> 00:00:29.670
You also hunt for straight lines and repeating patterns.

7
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:34.928
Maths is everywhere: in the market, in
the kitchen and on the way to school.

8
00:00:35.008 --> 00:00:41.224
By the end you will solve a number puzzle,
just like Amal and Sami do in this unit's story.

9
00:00:41.304 --> 00:00:47.035
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:47.115 --> 00:00:53.444
By the end of this unit, you will be able to
read and say big numbers, up to one million.

11
00:00:53.524 --> 00:00:59.565
You will also use the maths words addition,
subtraction, multiplication and division.

12
00:00:59.645 --> 00:01:05.397
You will also measure the size, height,
weight and distance of things around you.

13
00:01:05.477 --> 00:01:08.062
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

14
00:01:08.142 --> 00:01:14.666
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
number, million, fact, pattern, straight, addition.

15
00:01:14.746 --> 00:01:20.522
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

16
00:01:20.602 --> 00:01:25.517
The reading sequence includes Maths
Is Everywhere and A Pattern Poem.

17
00:01:25.597 --> 00:01:30.585
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

18
00:01:30.665 --> 00:01:34.929
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

19
00:01:35.009 --> 00:01:38.892
The first language focus is Present Simple and Imperatives.

20
00:01:38.972 --> 00:01:46.952
The Present Simple tells about things that happen often or
facts that are always true, like “The sun rises in the east.”

21
00:01:47.032 --> 00:01:51.587
An imperative is a command or
instruction, like “Measure the height.”

22
00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:55.483
Both help us speak and write clearly, especially in maths.

23
00:01:55.563 --> 00:01:59.849
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

24
00:01:59.929 --> 00:02:04.310
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 — Measure and Tell.

25
00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:07.966
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

26
00:02:08.046 --> 00:02:15.425
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

27
00:02:15.505 --> 00:02:17.142
You are ready to begin.

28
00:02:17.222 --> 00:02:24.386
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

29
00:02:24.466 --> 00:02:31.779
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
